   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_GBR_LOND_02">Euston Hotel,</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_GBR_LOND">London W.C.</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div> <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1922-08-24">24th August 1922</date>
                        </dateline> <salute>Dear Miss Weaver</salute>
                    </opener>     <p>I enclose <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">copy of a letter</seg> which I have sent to <name type="person" key="bors73">Doctor Borsch</name> and I hope you will approve of the step I have taken. <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">A word from him</seg>, if <choice>
                            <sic>professionnal</sic>
                            <corr>professional</corr>
                        </choice> etiquette allows him to give it in the circumstances, would have a calming effect on me and enable me to make up my mind what to do.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>With kindest regards,</salute>
                        <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">See typed letter<rs type="letter" key="L_68901"> to Dr Borsch of 24 August 1922</rs> (BL Add. 57346, 128), in which JJ asks Borsch’s second opinion, as the London doctors insisted on the urgency of an eye operation for fear that glaucoma might set in at any moment.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Although JJ returned to Paris in mid-September, Borsch remained on holiday until the beginning of October. Upon his return, Borsch contradicted English doctors who had warned JJ of imminent glaucoma. Instead, he advised JJ to undergo teeth extraction while on vacation in Nice, so as to undergo a minor eye operation upon his return to Paris (<name type="work">JJ</name> 537). </note>
            </div>
      </body>
